Session logs and per-analysis captures — contents not tracked in git (see .gitignore)
=====================================================================================

This file only keeps the directory in a fresh clone; everything else here is a per-run
artifact written by the application, never committed. The application also creates the
directory itself if it is missing (src/Logger/Core.py).

What lands here
---------------
    logger/log_<date>_<HH-MM-SS>.txt one session log per application start (Logger/Core.py)
    logger/log_<Hardware>.csv        the run summary, one row per run, named after the
                                     loaded configuration's hardware id (log_unconfigured.csv
                                     before one is loaded); an older column set is archived
                                     beside it rather than overwritten
    logger/captures/                 each analysis's capture set — the frames, annotated
                                     image, label mask, _objects.json and _understanding.txt,
                                     bounded to the newest 50 sets (UI/Capture.py)
    logger/station_events_exported.txt
                                     the ledger of session logs already exported to the daily
                                     station event files (Logger/Station_Events.py)
    logger/Station_Events/           the shipped directory of the daily station event files
                                     (General.Station_Events.Directory); tracked by its .gitkeep

Deleting the session logs between sessions loses nothing the application needs to start, but a log
not yet in the ledger has not been exported. Logger/Station_Events/ must exist for the shipped
configuration to load. Deleting the ledger makes the next start record every log already here as
exported without exporting it.
